# ─── Supabase (agent profiles) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to .env.local for local dev, and set the same three in Vercel.
# The site builds and runs fine WITHOUT these — the agent portal simply stays
# switched off (profile pages 404, account pages show a notice). Nothing else
# on danangmls.com depends on them.

# Project URL and publishable ("anon") key: Supabase dashboard → Project Settings → API.
# Safe to expose to the browser; every table is behind row level security.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Service role ("secret") key — SERVER ONLY. Bypasses row level security entirely.
# Never prefix this with NEXT_PUBLIC_, and never commit a real value.
# Only used to delete a spam account from the admin screen; everything else works
# without it (the "Hide profile" action is the no-key fallback).
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Optional. Only needed if auth emails must point somewhere other than the
# auto-detected origin (production danangmls.com / the Vercel preview URL).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000
